//
// The resident tail -- AN1 -> FFN -> AN2 as one segment with partial-sum
// staging (builders/tail_pipeline.py, a port of iron's addnorm_ffn; docs/plans
// 31 §2.2) -- on the device: the chain shape that exercises the up->down
// L1->L1 hop, the depth-2 L2 ring and the two-column reduction, and the
// layer's width 512x768x3072 band-serial (32 bands of 16 rows, one ELF), three
// dispatches each, every element within the rung's derived tolerance. First
// passed 2026-08-22 (devq 518 / 522); the deadlock it took to get here is in
// the builder's FOOTGUNS and is pinned hermetically by
// run_tail_pipeline_structure_tests.lit's clauses 11 and 12.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_tail_pipeline_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_tail_pipeline_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-tail-pipeline PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: RUNG VERDICT: PASS (chain [64x96x192 m16 k48 n96 d2 nb2] ['PASS', 'PASS', 'PASS'])
// CHECK: RUNG VERDICT: PASS (width [512x768x3072 m16 k192 n96 d4 nb2 band-serial x32 omit-pingpong=L2] ['PASS', 'PASS', 'PASS'])
